Z||000000||sjp777||04-12-2001||09:55 PM||||I'm recovering my lower door panels this weekend. Does anyone know how to disattach the carpeted lower panel from the vinyl upper, and how do the map pockets come off?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Max The Chainsaw||04-13-2001||12:37 AM||||The map pockets are held on by 4 nuts on the inside of the panel. As for the carpeting, just gotta work at it, the glue they put that on with is strong.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Took the carpet off my 85 GT (The car formally know as "Grape Ape....) and had panels made and covered with vinyl.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||04-15-2001||11:55 AM||||Well, the drivers side is done. Covered in black leather. Looks awesome, and the smell, mmmm leather. Took almost all day. What a colossal pita. What is that glue GM uses to attach the carpet to the door panel? That sh*t could hold the frame together. I wish I had some. My fingers are all burned from the hot glue gun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Oh well, one done one to go. Sniff sniff back to the garage.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||GoCartGuy||04-15-2001||08:33 PM||||BTW for all you replacing the carpet here's how to get the old stuff off.  First off spray throught the carpet a good soaking of WD-40  this'll loosen the carpet from the glue.  As far as getting the glue off...hair dryer and a putty knife.  As far as new stuff, use indoor/outdoor carpet adhesive for the front and tack the back with a hot glue gun.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
